# Repository ignore rules.
#
# Two jobs, and the second is the one that matters: this tree is a *method*, and it must
# never carry a target. Samples, dumps, captured memory, licence material and keys are all
# things that appear naturally while working and must never be committed.

# --- build and bytecode ------------------------------------------------------
*.class
*.jar
*.o
*.obj
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.lib
!skills/exe-reverse/scripts/**/*.c

# --- analysis artifacts: never commit a target or a capture of one -----------
# A sample, a dump or an extracted payload is data about someone else's software.
*.exe
*.dll
*.sys
*.ocx
*.cpl
*.scr
*.drv
*.efi
*.msi
*.msp
*.msix
*.appx
*.bin
*.dat
*.dump
*.dmp
*.core
*.raw
*.mem
*.img
*.vhd

# --- reverser databases and tool state --------------------------------------
*.idb
*.i64
*.til
*.nam
*.unp
*.map
*.rep
*.asm
*.lst

# --- licence material and credentials ---------------------------------------
# The point of the skill is to classify a mechanism, never to ship a key.
*.lic
*.licence
*.license
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.snk
*.pem
*.der
*.crt
*.jks
*.keystore
*.kdbx
*.kdb

# --- captures ---------------------------------------------------------------
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.saz
*.har
*.etl
*.etlx
*.trace
*.jsonl

# --- local scratch ----------------------------------------------------------
_tmp/
out/
work/
audit_out/
exports/
samples/
captures/
*.log

# The workbench: vendored toolchains, unpacked samples, dumps, scratch notes. Nothing under
# tools/ belongs to the repository -- the skill's own evidence record lives in
# docs/tool-verification/ and carries no target identity or vendored binaries.
tools/

# Local scratch: **any** top-level underscore-prefixed directory is a work area, not content.
#
# This is a pattern rather than a list on purpose. An explicit list is how a research directory
# reached the staging area once: the directory names are chosen by whatever the research needed,
# so a rule that enumerates them is a rule that has to be updated by the person least likely to
# remember. Measured: one such directory carried 37.5 MB of third-party sources, a crash dump and
# a build artefact with a developer's home path inside it, all one `git add -A` away from being
# committed to this repository.
/_*/
*.orig
*.rej

# sandbox installs made while testing `npx skills add .` against this repo
.claude/
.agents/
.opencode/
.cursor/

# --- python and editors -----------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- generated --------------------------------------------------------------
# Screenshots are evidence while a task runs and are never part of the tree; the text of what
# they show belongs in the record instead.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.bmp
*.gif
